  "subject": {
    "id": "subject-of-a-source-asserted-record",
    "type": "DOCUMENT"
  },
  "summary": "Carry what a source-asserted record is about as a subject reference, refuse a subject the sentence that asserts it does not name, and report subject coverage.",
  "why": "handover/2026-09-05-v42-rca.md, follow-up 1. Run-04 attached observations and claims to what they were about 27 times and answered 240 query rows, 94 of them resting on relations whose formalizing sentence names neither endpoint; run-08, the same model on the same reading, made no science relation, put the feature inside quantity_kind text 23 times in 131 observations, and answered 8. Neither the producer's ontology nor the pack offered a slot for what a record is about. research 0.5.0 adds optional single subject on the SourceAsserted mixin, ranged on Entity as a relation endpoint is, borrowed from RDF 1.1 Concepts with SOSA's feature of interest recorded as the narrower term passed over. The adapter refuses SUBJECT_NOT_NAMED, aggregated, when the subject's name, whitespace collapsed and case folded, is absent from every statement formalizing the record's subject path; the plan compiler refuses DANGLING_SUBJECT for a subject resolving in neither the change set nor the base state. The census gains subject_coverage, reported and never refused. Core-12's residuals close: DIGEST_NOT_LOCATED for a digest no locator can check, and _derivation_census loses an unread argument."
}
